cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FoveaXR in research or write about it, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "FoveaXR: foveated rendering for any PC VR game"
abstract: "Free, open-source foveated rendering for PC VR games: an OpenXR API layer and an OpenVR proxy that apply variable rate shading (Direct3D 12 VRS Tier 2, Direct3D 11 through NVAPI) to a game's eye passes, fixed or following eye tracking, with a tray app that enables it per game and measures the GPU time saved."
authors:
  - alias: EncidXVII
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/EncidXVII/FoveaXR"
url: "https://everyvr.net/foveaxr"
keywords:
  - virtual reality
  - foveated rendering
  - variable rate shading
  - eye tracking
  - OpenXR API layer
  - OpenVR
  - SteamVR
  - VR performance
